In contrast, task 'def' encompasses items y1 through y4—each displaying a tighter grouping in terms of both initiation and completion. Both y1 and y2 start on February 6, with y1 ending on February 20 and y2 on February 21. The items y3 and y4 initiate on February 7 and end on February 21 and 22 respectively, demonstrating substantial concurrency across the portfolio of items within this task. The heavy overlap may reflect a strategic approach to parallelization or synchronized dependencies among these deliverables.

The 'task.1' field introduces additional layering, where select items under task 'abc' are mapped directly to either 'abc' itself or to 'def,' while others, including those under task 'def,' are unmapped or marked as undefined. This may suggest the presence of cross-task relationships or follow-on assignments that do not correspond one-to-one with the original categorization.

