What emerges from this construction, however, is a matrix that cannot be immediately interpreted as a filled-out quantitative roster—many intersecting cells are absent of values, presenting instead as placeholders or labels. For example, the presence of “Total” at the end of the staff hierarchy implies an intention for aggregation, but actual counts or subtotals are notably missing. Similarly, the arrangement of months and quarters suggests an anticipated pattern of periodic tracking, but without population in the cells, any trend or variance analysis over quarters or years remains prospective rather than retrospective.

