Please extract the employee attendance records from Sheet1, including the Time In, Time Out, and corresponding attendance remarks based on the defined 08:30–17:30 standard shift. Format the data into JSON following the given structure that categorizes attendance as ON TIME, EARLY OUT, LATE ARRIVAL, or LATE ARRIVAL/EARLY OUT according to the specified criteria.

=== Report ===
The analysis focuses on patterns of employee attendance relative to a defined standard shift time. The established duty periods are fixed at a start time of 08:30 and an end time of 17:30. Attendance behavior is then assessed by comparing individual clock-ins and clock-outs against these benchmark times to categorize punctuality and deviations from expected work hours.

Employees arriving before or at 08:30 and leaving at or after 17:30 are considered "ON TIME," reflecting full adherence or voluntary extension beyond standard hours. When an employee arrives before the scheduled start but leaves earlier than 17:30, the status shifts to "EARLY OUT," indicating premature departure despite timely arrival.

Conversely, employees arriving after 08:30 and leaving after 17:30 are marked as "LATE ARRIVAL," signifying a delayed start that is not compensated by early departure. The final scenario covers cases where both arrival is late and departure is early relative to the scheduled times, categorized as "LATE ARRIVAL/EARLY OUT," a dual deviation pointing to reduced workplace presence during official hours.

These classifications offer a structured framework for evaluating timekeeping discipline and can be instrumental in understanding attendance trends, identifying potential productivity risks, and ensuring compliance with organizational policies. The following table aggregates these criteria alongside specific examples illustrating each case, demonstrating how various time entries map to the corresponding attendance remarks.

## Sheet: Sheet1

| Time In   | Time  Out   | Unnamed: 11                                                                                |
|:----------|:------------|:-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| nan       | nan         | actual duty Time_IN is: 08:30 (cell C8)                                                    |
| nan       | nan         | actual duty Time_OUT is: 17:30 (cell D8)                                                   |
| nan       | nan         | remarks column: (cell [Person_1])                                                          |
| 08:15:00  | 17:45:00    | f a person comes before or actual time in and gone after actual time out that is "ON TIME" |
| 08:15:00  | 17:15:00    | If a person comes before or actual time in but gone before time out that is "EARLY OUT"    |
| 08:45:00  | 18:15:00    | If a person comes after actual time in and gone after time out that is "LATE ARRIVAL"      |
| 08:45:00  | 17:15:00    | If a person denies both conditions that is "LATE ARRIVAL/EARLY OUT"                        |


To provide further perspective, the attendance scenarios can be summarized as follows:

| Arrival vs. 08:30 | Departure vs. 17:30 | Attendance Status          |
|-------------------|--------------------|---------------------------|
| On or before      | On or after        | ON TIME                   |
| On or before      | Before             | EARLY OUT                 |
| After             | On or after        | LATE ARRIVAL              |
| After             | Before             | LATE ARRIVAL/EARLY OUT    |

This framework simplifies the evaluation of an individual's daily attendance and enables consistent reporting and interpretation across departments. Understanding these patterns helps in making informed management decisions regarding work schedules and employee accountability.

