Beyond extraction, the next analytical step involves mapping these identified types against a predefined list of recognized item categories: "Top," "Bottom," "Outerwear," "Sets," and "Shoes," among others. This results in segmenting the extracted types into two groups: those that appear on the master list and those that do not. For example, in one illustration, “Outerwear” belongs to the standardized category set, while associated types like “Christmas” and “Festive” do not.

The applied logic can be summarized in tabular form, capturing both sides of this split — matched versus unmatched types per entry:

